assic 1940–44 version of the program, hosted by radio's Fred Allen, was followed by a radio series on ABC in the spring of 1948. When Texaco first took it to television on NBC on June 8, 1948, the show had a huge cultural impact.","popularity":2.2375,"poster_path":null,"first_air_date":"1948-06-08","softcore":false,"name":"Texaco Star Theater","vote_average":7.5,"vote_count":6},{"adult":false,"backdrop_path":"/7jEnft2CLNbILWAiBRIBrXNN7Qh.jpg","genre_ids":[10767,35],"id":498,"origin_country":["US"],"original_language":"en","original_name":"Late Show with David Letterman","overview":"David Letterman uses mature humor to appeal to his audience in this weeknight series, which gets its music from a house band led by Paul Shaffer. Among the show's most-famous segments are the Top Ten List and Stupid Pet Tricks, the latter of which subsequently led to an additional recurring segment called Stupid Human Tricks.","popularity":261.9975,"poster_path":"/fTBC5EpsgKmli9VQcJMtqQ08Qj4.jpg","first_air_date":"1993-08-30","softcore":false,"name":"Late Show with David Letterman","vote_average":6.466,"vote_count":175},{"adult":false,"backdrop_path":"/1AXZzbRl8Wxub63tRgySQiiix71.jpg","genre_ids":[10764,35],"id":499,"origin_country":["US"],"original_language":"en","original_name":"The Osbournes","overview":"The Osbournes is an American reality television program featuring the domestic life of heavy metal singer Ozzy Osbourne and his family. The series premiered on MTV on March 5, 2002, and in its first season, was cited as the most-viewed series ever on MTV. The final episode of the series aired March 21, 2005.","popularity":11.0889,"poster_path":"/kTqCW7e2YtK8DrSHb9FkYDuuhY9.jpg","first_air_date":"2002-03-05","softcore":false,"name":"The Osbournes","vote_average":6.2,"vote_count":60},{"adult":false,"backdrop_path":"/c8m4NAE774Vsn5AZvn2bFarUtDX.jpg","genre_ids":[16,10765,35,10751],"id":504,"origin_country":["CA","US"],"original_language":"en","original_name":"The Ren & Stimpy Show","overview":"Ren and Stimpy are a mismatch made in animation heaven with nothing in common but a life-long friendship and an incredible knack for getting into trouble. Join them in their bizarre and gross world for some outlandish situations coupled with hilarious jokes.","popularity":24.0889,"poster_path":"/u4YZhMms48mgP756hniUcw6PQPU.jpg","first_air_date":"1991-08-11","softcore":false,"name":"The Ren & Stimpy Show","vote_average":7.592,"vote_count":541},{"adult":false,"backdrop_path":"/gBeHadaylDePYy6Gy2xyDVeYLkP.jpg","genre_ids":[35,10765],"id":326,"origin_country":["GB"],"original_language":"en","original_name":"Red Dwarf","overview":"The adventures of the last human alive and his friends, stranded three million years into deep space on the mining ship Red Dwarf.","popularity":38.83,"poster_path":"/cU9RFlyvJXbzyCzCGRqRmZrTDZU.jpg","first_air_date":"1988-02-15","softcore":false,"name":"Red Dwarf","vote_average":8.1,"vote_count":465},{"adult":false,"backdrop_path":"/5GMxq17cOxKrzQypbHAVQWZ0eMD.jpg","genre_ids":[35],"id":380,"origin_country":["GB"],"original_language":"en","original_name":"Little Britain","overview":"A zany comedy show with Matt Lucas and David Walliams, featuring characters from all over Little Britain.","popularity":15.6874,"poster_path":"/d8ss1109kLq2Z4K1eO9575CCKBe.jpg","first_air_date":"2003-09-16","softcore":false,"name":"Little Britain","vote_average":7.1,"vote_count":264},{"adult":false,"backdrop_path":"/5GkRPoUZXiYPGQeOUUUC3zIbL4w.jpg","genre_ids":[35,10762],"id":376,"origin_country":["US"],"original_language":"en","original_name":"The Amanda Show","overview":"The Amanda Show is an American live action sketch comedy and variety show that aired on Nickelodeon from October 16, 1999 to September 21, 2002. It starred Amanda Bynes, Drake Bell, and Nancy Sullivan, along with several performing artists who came and left at different points, such as John Kassir, Raquel Lee, and Josh Peck. The show was a spin-off from All That, in which Bynes had co-starred for several years. The show was unexpectedly cancelled at the end of 2002, according to creator Dan Schneider's blog. Writers for the show included John Hoberg, Steven Molaro, Andrew Hill Newman, and Dan Schneider.\n\nTwo years after the end of The Amanda Show, Dan Schneider created a new series, called Drake & Josh, featuring Drake Bell, Josh Peck and Nancy Sullivan.","popularity":7.4527,"poster_path":"/qzoU9ACuhNZQ8IMhWPKAGXskGtr.jpg","first_air_date":"1999-10-16","softcore":false,"name":"The Amanda Show","vote_average":7.1,"vote_count":59},{"adult":false,"backdrop_path":"/vhU1AMY3x4QPL0LRGHS8dEYN75e.jpg","genre_ids":[16,35,10762],"id":557,"origin_country":["US"],"original_language":"en","original_name":"Camp Lazlo","overview":"The series is set in a universe inhabited solely by anthropomorphic animals of many species and focuses on a trio of campers attending a poorly run summer camp known as Camp Kidney. The trio consists of Lazlo, the eccentric, optimistic spider monkey; Raj, the timid Indian elephant; and Clam, the quiet albino pygmy rhinoceros, and their multiple surreal misadventures.","popularity":30.1978,"poster_path":"/9fZXdQbYeDMBTBtMNnsF2K2YWBh.jpg","first_air_date":"2005-07-08","softcore":false,"name":"Camp Lazlo","vote_average":6.9,"vote_count":169},{"adult":false,"backdrop_path":"/5yDNgSOWPbZq9wqmgegzWX9eFWA.jpg","genre_ids":[35],"id":29181,"origin_country":["DE"],"original_language":"de","original_name":"Otto - Die Serie","overview":"“Otto – The Series” is an unusual comedy format from the early 1990s centred on Otto Waalkes, blending classic crime entertainment with Otto’s distinctive brand of humour. Rather than telling a continuous story, the series combines newly shot sketches featuring Otto with scenes from old Edgar Wallace films. These original sequences were re-dubbed, completely transforming their content. Dialogue that was once serious turns into absurd wordplay, and the originally suspenseful plots are deliberately played for laughs. I